WEBVTT

00:05.800 --> 00:07.790
It's finally winter break.

00:07.870 --> 00:10.030
The principal's speech was long.

00:10.140 --> 00:11.370
About the people going skiing...

00:11.370 --> 00:13.070
Get ahold of yourself, my brother!

00:13.440 --> 00:15.910
A white... a white alligator...

00:20.410 --> 00:21.710
Mizuki!

00:22.780 --> 00:24.280
It's at eight tonight!

00:24.280 --> 00:26.580
Our long-awaited Christmas party.

00:26.650 --> 00:28.220
No canceling at the last minute, okay?

00:28.220 --> 00:30.280
I've already told them we're coming.

00:30.590 --> 00:32.060
Oh, okay.

00:37.960 --> 00:39.830
Comi-Pa is tomorrow!

00:40.030 --> 00:42.730
You really gonna be okay like this?

00:43.000 --> 00:45.560
Just barely. All I've got left is the finish.

00:47.940 --> 00:51.170
<i>I love them all. Doujinshi,</i> <i>exhibition and spot sales,</i>

00:52.110 --> 00:53.580
<i>and Kazuki, too.</i>

00:54.180 --> 00:58.670
<i>And I could work with Kazuki,</i> <i>makin' books and bein'a shopgirl.</i>

01:00.720 --> 01:03.020
So, what should we wear?

01:03.120 --> 01:05.110
Nothing too kiddy.
We're too old for that.

01:06.460 --> 01:08.550
That's true. Something mature would be nice.

01:08.630 --> 01:10.150
Yeah.

01:15.000 --> 01:16.630
Christmas...

01:18.940 --> 01:22.500
<i>Just be you and don't change.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Kawaranaide</i>

01:23.040 --> 01:26.140
<i>You're more precious to me than anyone.</i>
<i>Dare Yori mo Taisetsu na</i>

01:26.140 --> 01:29.710
<i>You have a great, sparkling dream...</i>
<i>Ohki na Yume Kagayakaseta</i>

01:29.950 --> 01:33.010
<i>...and you're my one and only friend.</i>
<i>Tada Hitori no Tomodachi</i>

01:33.280 --> 01:36.890
<i>It just doesn't get across...</i>
<i>Nani o Shite mo Tsutawarazu</i>

01:36.890 --> 01:40.460
<i>It's just not working right at all.</i>
<i>Umaku Ikanai Bakari de</i>

01:40.460 --> 01:43.830
<i>But even I and everyone else...</i>
<i>Watashi Datte Dare Datte</i>

01:44.030 --> 01:47.520
<i>... have times like that.</i>
<i>Atarimae ni Aru Koto</i>

01:47.630 --> 01:51.000
<i>Those things that don't return to your heart.</i>
<i>Mune no Naka ni Kaeranai</i>

01:51.200 --> 01:54.600
<i>But even those words and feelings...</i>
<i>Omoi mo Kotoba mo Itsuka</i>

01:54.770 --> 01:59.210
<i>... will come back in time someday...</i>
<i>Jikan ga Tateba Modotte Kuru kara</i>

01:59.410 --> 02:02.350
<i>... before you know it.</i>
<i>Shiranai Uchi ni</i>

02:02.610 --> 02:08.550
<i>There's only one thing you can do right now.</i>
<i>Ima Kimiga Dekiru Koto wa Hitotsu</i>

02:08.920 --> 02:15.620
<i>Just accept it and go with it.</i>
<i>Sono Mama Ukeirete Yukou</i>

02:16.260 --> 02:20.300
<i>Just be you and stay true to yourself.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Itsuwarazu ni</i>

02:20.300 --> 02:23.440
<i>Take a little break.</i>
<i>Sukoshi Hitoyasumi Shite</i>

02:23.440 --> 02:27.210
<i>Take your impatience and your hardships...</i>
<i>Aseru Kimochi Kurushii Koto</i>

02:27.210 --> 02:30.470
<i>...and turn them into your strengths.</i>
<i>Kimi no Power ni Kaete</i>

02:30.540 --> 02:34.310
<i>Just be you and don't change.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Kawaranaide</i>

02:34.680 --> 02:37.780
<i>You're more precious to me than anyone.</i>
<i>Dare Yori mo Taisetsu na</i>

02:37.780 --> 02:41.380
<i>You have a great, sparkling dream...</i>
<i>Ohki na Yume Kagayakaseta</i>

02:41.590 --> 02:44.490
<i>...and you're my one and only friend.</i>
<i>Tada Hitori no Tomodachi</i>

02:47.490 --> 02:54.300
OUR PARTY!

02:54.930 --> 02:56.930
Well, I'll see you all next year.

02:57.040 --> 02:59.060
Don't goof off too much.

03:00.370 --> 03:02.670
Rise! Bow!

03:08.950 --> 03:10.280
Let's go, comrade!

03:10.480 --> 03:12.140
Once you get through today...

03:13.220 --> 03:15.120
Ventriloquism comes to every gate with laughter!

03:15.120 --> 03:16.450
Yeah!

03:17.590 --> 03:20.020
Wait.

03:20.160 --> 03:22.630
Comrade, you conserve your energy.

03:22.760 --> 03:28.100
I shall be your Thunderbolt! Neigh!

03:28.470 --> 03:30.230
Hey, Taishi...

03:32.670 --> 03:34.500
My sister, what about you?

03:34.740 --> 03:36.400
I'll go after I get some stuff ready.

03:36.640 --> 03:39.510
Roger! Emergency launch! Scramble!

03:39.710 --> 03:43.270
Releasing the limiter and...
Varoom!

03:49.650 --> 03:50.450
Mizuki!

03:50.990 --> 03:52.390
We'll see you later!

03:52.460 --> 03:54.930
If you can't find the place, give me a call on my cell.

03:54.990 --> 03:56.260
Oh, okay.

03:56.900 --> 03:58.730
You think anyone cool will show up?

03:59.960 --> 04:01.300
Mizuki.

04:02.000 --> 04:03.700
You goin' to a Christmas party?

04:04.370 --> 04:05.200
Yeah.

04:05.600 --> 04:08.510
I see. Well, have fun. Later.

04:16.410 --> 04:20.220
O wind! O light! Grant us completion of our manuscript!

04:20.520 --> 04:23.920
Fight! Fight! Ka-zu-ki!

04:24.260 --> 04:25.490
Don't give up, Kazuki!

04:25.490 --> 04:28.790
V! V! V! Come on, victory!

04:29.160 --> 04:31.730
Taishi, you know, could you be a little more quiet?!

04:31.730 --> 04:33.560
Why, my brother?!

04:33.830 --> 04:38.390
I am sending you the passionate aura that I mastered in Asahi's fanclub!

04:38.770 --> 04:40.710
No, well, like I'm saying...

04:40.710 --> 04:41.930
Oh, I see!

04:42.010 --> 04:44.700
You would rather I help you with the finish instead of cheering for you.

04:44.780 --> 04:46.180
Forgive me.

04:45.440 --> 04:46.770
No, that's not what I meant...

04:46.980 --> 04:48.880
Leave pasting tones up to me!

04:49.080 --> 04:51.680
Finally, the time has come for me to show off...

04:51.750 --> 04:54.080
...my three-finger arpeggio pressure-sticking method!

04:54.320 --> 04:55.790
Wait! Wait!

04:56.120 --> 04:57.320
Thanks for waitin'!

04:58.620 --> 05:00.830
You're still doing last-minute work on your manuscript?!

05:00.830 --> 05:03.260
Lame! Super-lame!

05:03.430 --> 05:05.400
So, this is Mr. Kazuki's...

05:06.700 --> 05:09.130
Eimi! And Miss Aya, too!

05:09.300 --> 05:11.330
I called them and had 'em come over!

05:11.470 --> 05:13.300
The more help the better, right?

05:27.150 --> 05:28.450
6 o'clock...

05:53.280 --> 05:55.080
Done!

05:55.580 --> 05:58.150
You have done well, my brother!

05:57.350 --> 06:00.890
Kazuki! Yay! Kazuki!

06:00.390 --> 06:03.350
I have all of you to thank for this! Thank you!

06:04.990 --> 06:06.150
So, how is it?

06:06.220 --> 06:07.330
How's what?

06:07.330 --> 06:10.490
Did you end up with somethin' you really wanted to draw?

06:13.630 --> 06:15.330
I think so.

06:16.670 --> 06:20.800
At least, this is the very best manuscript I can draw right now.

06:21.070 --> 06:22.940
I've done my very best.

06:23.340 --> 06:27.340
I've drawn what I think is the most interesting. So...

06:27.850 --> 06:28.510
So?

06:29.180 --> 06:33.520
I won't have any regrets, even if it doesn't sell a single copy.

06:34.320 --> 06:36.580
Okay then, that's good.

06:36.950 --> 06:38.190
I guess!

06:38.190 --> 06:41.060
I think you've gotten a little better than before.

06:41.190 --> 06:43.720
Just a little though, just a little.

06:44.530 --> 06:45.860
It was good.

06:46.600 --> 06:49.230
I only read it as I was helping out,

06:49.930 --> 06:51.840
but it was really good.

06:52.670 --> 06:54.640
O-okay. Thanks.

06:54.970 --> 06:56.840
But the real work's still ahead!

06:56.940 --> 06:58.200
Exactly!

06:58.380 --> 07:01.750
At 32 pages, it has a lot of pages for a photocopied book these days.

07:01.750 --> 07:04.650
And we must make 50 copies!

07:04.780 --> 07:06.380
This is "do or die" time!

07:06.520 --> 07:08.380
Like the Battle in the
Rainbow Star Cluster!

07:08.820 --> 07:10.810
D'you make the arrangement for the goods?

07:11.420 --> 07:13.250
They will be here shortly!

07:17.930 --> 07:20.730
Hey, it's snowing!

07:22.170 --> 07:23.430
Snow (yuki)?

07:24.540 --> 07:26.900
I'm Yuki Morikawa!

07:27.270 --> 07:29.330
His meaning is lost on me.

07:37.650 --> 07:38.950
She's here.

07:39.020 --> 07:40.450
Let us go, comrade!

07:40.450 --> 07:41.610
Yeah!

07:43.960 --> 07:45.450
I cannot stop!

07:47.060 --> 07:48.120
Fight!

07:48.260 --> 07:49.450
One shot!

07:54.600 --> 07:55.870
Comrade!

07:55.330 --> 07:55.990
Right!

08:00.870 --> 08:02.100
A two-step throw!

08:09.310 --> 08:11.150
P-please pardon me.

08:11.320 --> 08:13.080
Chisa, are you okay?

08:13.180 --> 08:14.620
Yes, I am fine!

08:15.150 --> 08:18.150
And now, the weapon for our final showdown has arrived!

08:18.290 --> 08:20.380
Then let's get started!

08:28.430 --> 08:30.030
We're making good progress!

08:30.100 --> 08:33.800
Yes! Mr. Copy Machine is in a better mood than usual!

08:34.370 --> 08:38.000
It must have taken a liking to your manuscript!

08:45.780 --> 08:48.010
It seems our progress has been too good, and we ran out of paper!

08:48.120 --> 08:49.990
Wait! I will refill it right away!

08:53.160 --> 08:54.280
Maybe it's a paper jam?

08:56.790 --> 08:59.300
Mr. Copy Machine worked too hard...

08:58.730 --> 09:01.330
REPLACE TONER

08:59.300 --> 09:01.330
...and it seems to have run out of toner!

09:01.330 --> 09:02.770
What?!

09:03.570 --> 09:05.070
Let's get more toner!

09:05.070 --> 09:07.130
We do not have any in stock!

09:07.210 --> 09:08.470
Then call the service center!

09:08.770 --> 09:10.330
This is the number, right?!

09:10.510 --> 09:12.910
<i>We are closed for the day.</i>

09:13.710 --> 09:18.240
<i>Our business hours on</i> <i>weekdays are from 9am to 5pm.</i>

09:18.720 --> 09:20.840
<i>We appreciate your call.</i>

09:23.050 --> 09:25.390
It says they're closed already...

09:33.400 --> 09:36.130
No! Since it's come to this, we will use our last resort!

09:36.300 --> 09:37.000
What?!

09:37.370 --> 09:39.340
We have no choice but to go out into town...

09:39.340 --> 09:41.400
...and make copies at various convenience stores!

09:47.280 --> 09:48.970
Comrade Kazuki and you two go that way!

09:49.110 --> 09:51.410
We will go this way! Spread out!

09:55.920 --> 09:57.090
Welcome.

09:57.090 --> 09:58.520
Where's your copy machine?

09:57.820 --> 09:58.920
Over there, Sir.

09:59.260 --> 10:01.350
That character is so cool, you know?

10:01.460 --> 10:03.330
Yeah, do you know who did his voice?

10:03.330 --> 10:06.990
The Wait Is Over!

10:03.330 --> 10:06.990
Nishimu News

10:03.330 --> 10:06.990
Year-End Special

10:03.560 --> 10:05.500
Masami Kikuchi? Kouichi Touchika?

10:07.370 --> 10:11.560
Oh, right. It's tomorrow.
Everyone's out making copies.

10:12.640 --> 10:13.900
Eight o'clock.

10:38.830 --> 10:40.160
How many more?

10:39.700 --> 10:41.190
About thirty copies.

10:41.900 --> 10:43.330
No good here.

10:43.400 --> 10:45.600
Anyway, I gotta find a free copy machine!

10:57.180 --> 11:00.780
Let's see, convenience store, convenience store...

11:05.460 --> 11:09.290
I'm number one in sales, and now I'll be number one in getting the copies made!

11:09.560 --> 11:10.930
D'oh.

11:10.130 --> 11:12.100
OUT

11:10.130 --> 11:12.100
OF

11:10.130 --> 11:12.100
ORDER

11:12.100 --> 11:14.460
That's just sassy for a copy machine!

11:14.530 --> 11:16.330
Who do you think I am?!

11:16.770 --> 11:18.570
Take this and this and this and this and this...

11:18.570 --> 11:20.340
...and this and this and this and this...

11:18.940 --> 11:20.340
Excuse me, Miss...

11:20.710 --> 11:23.400
What?! I'm busy and you want an autograph?!

11:23.640 --> 11:25.470
Oh, fine!

11:41.490 --> 11:44.550
Convenience store search radar, activating at full power!

11:45.130 --> 11:46.500
Ping! Ping!

11:46.500 --> 11:48.300
Mother, what's that?

11:46.530 --> 11:48.960
Ping! Ping!

11:49.500 --> 11:51.770
Poor thing. And it's Christmas, too.

11:52.100 --> 11:53.800
Whoosh!

12:03.810 --> 12:07.950
Because... Because of
Chisa, his book may fail!

12:08.090 --> 12:10.520
I must quickly find a
Mr. Convenience Store!

12:15.660 --> 12:16.890
Are you okay?

12:17.360 --> 12:19.260
Oh, Miss Mizuki!

12:19.330 --> 12:20.060
Chisa?

12:20.360 --> 12:22.330
Y-you saved me.

12:22.800 --> 12:26.070
Thanks to you, I have been able to keep his manuscript clean!

12:26.770 --> 12:29.070
His? Do you mean Kazuki's?

12:29.440 --> 12:33.810
Yes! We have no time, so everyone split up to go make copies!

12:34.210 --> 12:35.300
Everyone?

12:35.680 --> 12:37.810
Oh, no! I must hurry!

12:38.080 --> 12:40.280
Well, thank you very much!

13:00.340 --> 13:02.810
Reserved for Today

13:10.150 --> 13:11.680
You're late, Mizuki!

13:11.680 --> 13:13.310
Over here, over here!

13:21.660 --> 13:23.560
I-I'm done!

13:26.030 --> 13:28.090
Every place was so crowded,

13:28.330 --> 13:31.790
I ended up havin' to go really far out.

13:32.340 --> 13:33.640
Chisa, too.

13:33.640 --> 13:35.040
Likewise.

13:35.340 --> 13:37.640
It just ticks me off!

13:37.840 --> 13:40.840
I, the great, cute Eimi, wanted to make copies!

13:41.580 --> 13:44.410
With all this, it's already past 11?

13:44.750 --> 13:45.620
Oh...

13:45.620 --> 13:46.810
What is it?

13:46.880 --> 13:49.850
Oh, yeah, the train service'll end soon.

13:51.890 --> 13:53.150
Everyone, thank you.

13:53.690 --> 13:55.350
It looks like we'll make it in time,

13:55.430 --> 13:57.490
so Taishi and I will do the rest.

13:57.600 --> 13:58.760
What?

13:58.900 --> 14:00.230
Are you super-for real?!

14:00.230 --> 14:03.670
You have to fold the copies and staple them together!

14:04.370 --> 14:06.430
Chisa will help out, too!

14:07.540 --> 14:10.410
But you all need to get ready for tomorrow too, right?

14:10.640 --> 14:13.510
And the trains might stop because of the snow.

14:14.010 --> 14:16.040
You should hurry on home.

14:18.780 --> 14:21.690
There's plenty of time until I have to submit it in the morning.

14:21.950 --> 14:23.120
I'll be fine, now.

14:23.120 --> 14:26.090
Reserved for Today

14:41.310 --> 14:43.000
Mi-zu-ki!

14:44.510 --> 14:46.310
You're going to the after party, right?!

14:46.310 --> 14:48.110
They're going to karaoke!

14:49.110 --> 14:50.840
But, it's already late.

14:51.150 --> 14:54.550
Don't worry! He's got a car.

14:54.950 --> 14:57.440
I'll drive you home if it ends up getting a little late.

14:59.860 --> 15:01.690
You'll go, won't you? Um...

15:02.060 --> 15:04.690
Oh, I'm Mizuki. Mizuki Takase.

15:05.200 --> 15:08.960
Speaking of karaoke, that last time was just out there.

15:09.400 --> 15:11.430
Yeah, Sudoh's friend, right?

15:11.570 --> 15:15.940
I complained to Sudoh afterward about inviting a guy like that.

15:16.040 --> 15:18.440
What? Did something happen?

15:18.810 --> 15:20.680
Well, it's not like the guy was a kid,

15:20.780 --> 15:23.270
but he kept on singing nothing but anime and monster film songs.

15:23.350 --> 15:24.680
No way!

15:24.080 --> 15:24.710
For real!

15:25.380 --> 15:28.910
He was yelling "Boom!" and "Bam!"...

15:29.220 --> 15:31.450
...and then he started singing those kinds of songs.

15:31.720 --> 15:33.390
Whoa, creepy!

15:33.390 --> 15:34.430
Right?

15:34.430 --> 15:35.830
I guess it's called doujinshi.

15:35.890 --> 15:39.300
He seems to have formed one of those weird groups.

15:40.060 --> 15:42.300
Oh, I saw that during our school festival!

15:42.570 --> 15:44.330
He had all these anime signs lined up...

15:44.470 --> 15:46.800
...and he was calling to customers wearing a costume he'd made!

15:47.300 --> 15:49.100
Yeah, and sweating like a pig.

15:49.210 --> 15:52.470
It's awful!
It ruins our school's image.

15:52.680 --> 15:54.410
Like we had any of that to begin with!

16:00.720 --> 16:02.280
What's the matter?

16:02.390 --> 16:03.050
I...

16:04.390 --> 16:06.120
I don't really know,

16:06.490 --> 16:09.760
but I don't like to hear people being ridiculed...

16:10.230 --> 16:12.130
...when they're working so hard at something.

16:12.260 --> 16:14.030
Oh, did we upset you?

16:14.030 --> 16:16.090
But don't you think it's seriously creepy?

16:16.730 --> 16:18.290
But... But...

16:19.840 --> 16:22.070
I like people who work really hard at something,

16:22.240 --> 16:26.870
no matter what people around them think!

16:29.080 --> 16:31.810
I don't want to hear them being ridiculed!

16:37.720 --> 16:40.020
Chinami, Reina, I'm sorry.

17:01.350 --> 17:04.320
Yuu, shouldn't you head home soon, too?

17:04.850 --> 17:08.010
It's okay, I brought my stuff with me.

17:08.550 --> 17:12.250
I can go straight to the convention hall from here tomorrow.

17:19.830 --> 17:21.230
Wonderful!

17:22.300 --> 17:25.830
Wonderful, my comrade!
This book will be...

17:29.710 --> 17:31.010
Now...

17:32.010 --> 17:33.440
How are you doing?

17:33.010 --> 17:34.940
I've got about half of them folded.

17:35.450 --> 17:37.710
Okay, just a little more to go, then.

17:57.230 --> 18:00.170
Everyone's tired from the copy machine commotion.

18:17.620 --> 18:18.520
Mizuki...

18:18.990 --> 18:21.150
You're almost done. Right, Kazuki?

18:25.930 --> 18:27.830
I can't draw,

18:30.070 --> 18:32.060
but I can at least help you with this.

18:43.810 --> 18:45.410
Why are you here?

18:45.920 --> 18:48.940
I went to a Christmas party with my friends,

18:50.020 --> 18:51.780
but I didn't have any fun there.

18:52.220 --> 18:53.020
Why?

18:55.460 --> 18:57.020
Because you weren't there.

18:57.460 --> 18:58.260
What?

19:01.300 --> 19:02.770
Say, you know something, Kazuki?

19:04.670 --> 19:07.430
Miracles happen on the night of Christmas Eve.

19:08.010 --> 19:11.000
So, your book is definitely going to be on time, Kazuki!

19:14.140 --> 19:15.340
Yeah.

19:16.150 --> 19:18.880
Mizuki, take care of these.
Organize the pages.

19:20.020 --> 19:20.610
Okay.

19:24.720 --> 19:27.780
<i>They're such a troublesome couple.</i>

19:38.870 --> 19:40.170
Done!

19:41.040 --> 19:42.700
You did it, Kazuki!

19:43.740 --> 19:47.340
It's exactly like you said,
Mizuki. It's a miracle.

19:50.410 --> 19:51.940
Look at the time already.

19:53.450 --> 19:54.450
Wow!

19:54.450 --> 19:55.980
What is it?

20:06.360 --> 20:07.420
What?

20:07.530 --> 20:09.470
What's going to happen to Comi-Pa?!

20:09.600 --> 20:12.070
It's okay! There's nothin' to worry about!

20:12.540 --> 20:13.440
Precisely!

20:14.340 --> 20:18.110
You will see when you get there, my brother, my sister.

20:28.020 --> 20:29.040
Ladies and gentlemen,

20:29.420 --> 20:32.290
it is very slippery here due to the snow,

20:32.360 --> 20:34.520
so please be careful as you stand in line!

20:35.130 --> 20:39.530
We cannot allow our festival to be deterred by mere snow!

20:39.800 --> 20:42.600
This snow is nothing, this puny snow!

20:46.640 --> 20:48.200
See? Look at that.

20:48.310 --> 20:49.310
Wow!

20:49.310 --> 20:51.780
I think there might be more people here than the one in the summer.

20:51.980 --> 20:55.000
It doesn't matter whether there's a snowstorm or a hurricane.

20:55.380 --> 20:57.310
If you come here, everyone will be here.

20:57.380 --> 20:59.320
If you come here, you can meet everyone.

20:59.850 --> 21:01.610
Staff members, shopgirls and shopboys, and customers.

21:01.820 --> 21:03.810
Everyone's thinkin' the same thing.

21:04.620 --> 21:08.290
That's why they all carry their heavy bags and gather here.

21:09.630 --> 21:11.330
No matter how much it snows,

21:11.330 --> 21:15.700
the burnin' passion in our hearts can't be extinguished.

21:16.130 --> 21:20.260
I see. Everyone works really hard at this.

21:20.870 --> 21:22.170
Mizuki.

21:22.810 --> 21:26.070
You worked hard, too, together with Kazuki.

21:26.440 --> 21:27.600
What?

21:27.710 --> 21:28.840
Mizuki.

21:29.380 --> 21:31.750
Let's start it. Our party!

21:34.450 --> 21:35.350
Yeah!

21:35.420 --> 21:36.720
All right!

21:37.190 --> 21:41.180
The curtain is truly about to rise on the history of Brother 2!

21:42.060 --> 21:46.960
Comrade Kazuki and Comrade
Mizuki! Let us move out!

21:47.230 --> 21:48.220
Yeah!

21:49.800 --> 21:55.100
<i>We will now be opening the</i> <i>second Comic Party to the public.</i>

22:20.760 --> 22:24.970
<i>The distant sky looked bright...</i>
<i>Touku no Sora ga Akaruku Mieta</i>

22:24.970 --> 22:29.460
<i>...and we began walking.</i>
<i>Soshite Bokura wa Arukihajimeta</i>

22:29.610 --> 22:34.010
<i>Getting our feet caught in the mud.</i>
<i>Nukarumi ni Ashi o Torarenagara</i>

22:34.180 --> 22:38.050
<i>Heading for a shapeless city.</i>
<i>Katachi no Nai Machi o Mezashite</i>

22:38.050 --> 22:42.190
<i>The pocket in my heart was full...</i>
<i>Kokoro no Naka no Pocket ni wa</i>

22:42.190 --> 22:46.450
<i>...of the grownup things we'd just learned.</i>
<i>Oboetate no Otona ga Ippai</i>

22:46.620 --> 22:51.030
<i>Having taken off our uniforms...</i>
<i>Seifuku o Nuida Bokura ni wa</i>

22:51.160 --> 22:55.200
<i>... the wind was just a little too cold.</i>
<i>Kaze wa Sukoshi Tsumetasugita</i>

22:55.200 --> 22:58.770
<i>Who in the world am I?</i>
<i>Ittai Boku wa Dare Darou</i>

22:58.770 --> 23:03.670
<i>I think about that every so often.</i>
<i>Tokidoki Sonna Koto o Omou</i>

23:03.840 --> 23:07.340
<i>In the world outside the school building...</i>
<i>Kousha no Soto no Sekai de wa</i>

23:07.340 --> 23:12.750
<i>...it's like everyone is a</i> <i>pawn in a game of chess.</i>
<i>Daremo ga Marude Chess no Koma sa</i>

23:13.850 --> 23:18.290
<i>I'm here for you.</i>
<i>Kimi no Tame ni Boku ga Ite</i>

23:18.290 --> 23:22.290
<i>And you for me.</i>
<i>Boku no Tame ni Kimiga</i>

23:22.290 --> 23:26.830
<i>When you think about that...</i>
<i>Sou Omoeba Daremo ga</i>

23:26.830 --> 23:35.800
<i>... everyone is needed by someone.</i>
<i>Dareka no Tame ni Hitsuyou sa</i>
